  SUMMARY ADC alone typ ref=cref (frame 2 of 2): 12 conversions | theta -31.76 LSB (keep <=> plate-ref < theta; decision overlap 2.80 LSB), alpha 0.9811, c0 -0.82 LSB | code - ideal code: mean -32.25, range -34..-31 | transition offset T: mean +32.84 LSB, at mid-scale +32.85, slope +0.71 LSB/V = gain error -0.057 % | DAC-side INL 
  RESULT B: every conversion converges; the flat LVS cells convert like the design netlists apart from ONE uniform shift: codes -3 .. -1 LSB, transition offset T +2.76 .. +2.92 LSB (spread over the 12 inputs 0.16 LSB)  -> PASS (limits: |code change| <= 4 LSB, spread <= 0.5 LSB)
  The shift has three causes: Cxa 40 fF ideal -> 54.52 fF MIM unit, the 14 x 2 fF Cpb / Cpm removed, and NO diffusion parameters in an LVS netlist (PDK default ad = as = pd = ps = 0).
  Separated on the design netlists (AFE/adc/sim/f1_x2_inl_step.log, typ): Cxa alone moves the code offset by +1.5 LSB, Cpb / Cpm by +0.1 LSB; the rest (about -3.4 LSB) is the missing junction capacitance.

